  "term": "stereotypy",
  "definition": "Stereotypy refers to abnormal, repetitive behavior that appears to have no clear goal or purpose. In the supplied source, it is described as a form of abnormal repetitive behavior seen in captive animals and noted to resemble similar behaviors documented in people with neurodevelopmental disorders.",
